<title>USA: GM's Residential Asset files $2 bln shelf.</title>
<headline>GM's Residential Asset files $2 bln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Residential Asset Securities Corp, a unit of General Motors Corp's GMAC Mortgage, filed Monday a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $2 billion in mortgage and manufactured housing contract pass through certificates.</p>
<p>When combined with a previous registration, Residential Asset will have a total offering of $2,441,716,769.05 in certificates available for sale.  </p>
<p>Net proceeds will be used to repay short term loans or for general corporate purposes, among others, the company said in the filing.</p>
</text>
